IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-interpretation.l4 -- section 321 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the definitions "In this Part," (Part IX).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in parentheses
-- at the end of a defined term are quoted inside the quotation lines and are not encoded.
--
-- READING A RESULT. Every function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the facts bring the case within the term on the text's own words.
-- JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words ("means" and the case is outside it; a flat negative such as "does not include").
-- NOTHING: the text does not answer (a term it leaves to another provision, or an "includes" that does not close the list).
-- Every JUST FALSE carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"`, every NOTHING `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The terms are scoped "In this Part" (Part IX, ss 321 to 378): other Parts define the same words for themselves.

§ `Section 321 -- Definitions ("In this Part,")`

-- break means (a) to break any part, internal or external, or (b) to open any thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an internal or external opening.
-- src:6516 | break means
-- src:6517 | (a) to break any part, internal or external, or
-- src:6518 | (b) to open any thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an internal or external opening; (effraction)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "break" (src:6516-6518)
GIVEN `the person broke any part, internal or external` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person opened a thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an internal or external opening` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the person breaks` MEANS
    IF    `the person broke any part, internal or external`
       OR `the person opened a thing that is used or intended to be used to close or to cover an internal or external opening`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "break means"

-- credit card means any card, plate, coupon book or other device issued or otherwise distributed for the purpose of being used (a) on presentation to obtain, on credit, money, goods, services or any other thing of value, or (b) in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain any of the services offered through the machine, unit or device.
-- src:6519 | credit card means any card, plate, coupon book or other device issued or otherwise distributed for the purpose of being used
-- src:6520 | (a) on presentation to obtain, on credit, money, goods, services or any other thing of value, or
-- src:6521 | (b) in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain any of the services offered through the machine, unit or device; (carte de crédit)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "credit card" (src:6519-6521)
GIVEN `it is a card, plate, coupon book or other device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was issued or otherwise distributed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is that it be used on presentation to obtain, on credit, money, goods, services or any other thing of value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is that it be used in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain any of the services offered through the machine, unit or device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the thing is a credit card` MEANS
    IF    `it is a card, plate, coupon book or other device`
      AND `it was issued or otherwise distributed`
      AND (   `the purpose is that it be used on presentation to obtain, on credit, money, goods, services or any other thing of value`
           OR `the purpose is that it be used in an automated teller machine, a remote service unit or a similar automated banking device to obtain any of the services offered through the machine, unit or device`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "credit card means any card, plate, coupon book or other device issued or otherwise distributed for the purpose of being used"

-- document means any paper, parchment or other material on which is recorded or marked anything capable of being read or understood by a person, computer system or other device, and includes a credit card, but does not include trademarks on articles of commerce or inscriptions on stone or metal or other like material.
-- "Means ... and includes ..." is read as closed (fork F2 of the keel, taken here too): the means part plus the credit card; anything else is JUST FALSE.
-- src:6522 | document means any paper, parchment or other material on which is recorded or marked anything that is capable of being read or understood by a person, computer system or other device, and includes a credit card, but does not include trademarks on articles of commerce or inscriptions on stone or metal or other like material; (document)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "document" (src:6522)
GIVEN `it is paper, parchment or other material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `anything capable of being read or understood by a person, computer system or other device is recorded or marked on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a credit card, by s 321 the thing is a credit card` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a trademark on an article of commerce, or an inscription on stone or metal or other like material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the thing is a document` MEANS
    IF `it is a trademark on an article of commerce, or an inscription on stone or metal or other like material`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include trademarks on articles of commerce or inscriptions on stone or metal or other like material"
    ELSE `ccc12 or`
             (JUST (`it is paper, parchment or other material` AND `anything capable of being read or understood by a person, computer system or other device is recorded or marked on it`))
             `it is a credit card, by s 321 the thing is a credit card`
         -- JUST TRUE: "document means any paper, parchment or other material on which is recorded or marked anything" or "includes a credit card"
         -- JUST FALSE (neither limb, the credit card answer being a definite no): FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "document means any paper, parchment or other material on which is recorded or marked anything"
         -- NOTHING when the paper limb fails and the credit card answer is itself NOTHING: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the credit card answer was not given

-- exchequer bill means a bank-note, bond, note, debenture or security that is issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province.
-- src:6523 | exchequer bill means a bank-note, bond, note, debenture or security that is issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province; (bon du Trésor)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "exchequer bill" (src:6523)
DECLARE `s 321 exchequer bill kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 321 a bank-note`
    `s 321 a bond`
    `s 321 a note`
    `s 321 a debenture`
    `s 321 a security`
    `s 321 an instrument of another kind`

@ref Criminal Code s 321 "exchequer bill" (src:6523)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 321 exchequer bill kind`
      `it is issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the thing is an exchequer bill` MEANS
    IF `it is issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 321 a bank-note` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 321 a bond` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 321 a note` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 321 a debenture` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 321 a security` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 321 an instrument of another kind` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "exchequer bill means a bank-note, bond, note, debenture or security"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is issued or guaranteed by Her Majesty under the authority of Parliament or the legislature of a province"

-- exchequer bill paper means paper that is used to manufacture exchequer bills.
-- src:6524 | exchequer bill paper means paper that is used to manufacture exchequer bills; (papier de bons du Trésor)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "exchequer bill paper" (src:6524)
GIVEN `it is paper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used to manufacture exchequer bills` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the paper is exchequer bill paper` MEANS
    IF `it is paper` AND `it is used to manufacture exchequer bills`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "exchequer bill paper means paper that is used to manufacture exchequer bills"

-- false document means a document (a) the whole or a material part of which purports to be made by or on behalf of a person (i) who did not make it or authorize it to be made, or (ii) who did not in fact exist, (b) that is made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it but is false in some material particular, (c) that is made in the name of an existing person, by him or under his authority, with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made.
-- The three paragraphs are alternatives (the text lists them as separate cases of "a document"); the fork register records that the text has no "or" between them.
-- src:6525 | false document means a document
-- src:6526 | (a) the whole or a material part of which purports to be made by or on behalf of a person
-- src:6527 | (i) who did not make it or authorize it to be made, or
-- src:6528 | (ii) who did not in fact exist,
-- src:6529 | (b) that is made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it but is false in some material particular,
-- src:6530 | (c) that is made in the name of an existing person, by him or under his authority, with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made; (faux document)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "false document" (src:6525-6530)
GIVEN `it is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the whole or a material part of it purports to be made by or on behalf of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person did not make it or authorize it to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person did not in fact exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is false in some material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in the name of an existing person, by him or under his authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the document is a false document` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `it is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document` (JUST (`para (a)` OR `para (b)` OR `para (c)`))
    -- JUST TRUE: a document within one of paragraphs (a), (b) or (c).
    -- JUST FALSE when no paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "false document means a document"
    -- NOTHING only when the paragraphs hold and the document answer is NOTHING: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the document answer was not given
    WHERE
        `para (a)` MEANS
                `the whole or a material part of it purports to be made by or on behalf of a person`
            AND (   `that person did not make it or authorize it to be made`
                 OR `that person did not in fact exist`)
        `para (b)` MEANS
                `it is made by or on behalf of the person who purports to make it`
            AND `it is false in some material particular`
        `para (c)` MEANS
                `it is made in the name of an existing person, by him or under his authority`
            AND `it is made with a fraudulent intention that it should pass as being made by a person, real or fictitious, other than the person who makes it or under whose authority it is made`

-- revenue paper means paper that is used to make stamps, licences or permits or for any purpose connected with the public revenue.
-- src:6531 | revenue paper means paper that is used to make stamps, licences or permits or for any purpose connected with the public revenue. (papier de revenu)
@ref Criminal Code s 321 "revenue paper" (src:6531)
GIVEN `it is paper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used to make stamps, licences or permits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used for a purpose connected with the public revenue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 321 the paper is revenue paper` MEANS
    IF `it is paper` AND (`it is used to make stamps, licences or permits` OR `it is used for a purpose connected with the public revenue`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "revenue paper means paper that is used to make stamps, licences or permits or for any purpose connected with the public revenue"
